# Intent: tune the shake (host log 2026-10-21: a lift-and-shake by hand produced no event). The shake detector sums the change in the three axes between samples 100 ms apart and needs three peaks above a threshold within a second; the stock threshold of 16 m/s^2 needed a hard shake. It is now 9. Every shake reports its strongest peak (shake_peak event, "peak" and "threshold") and once a minute the strongest sample-to-sample change seen is reported (imu_stats, "max_diff" and "shakes"), so the threshold can be tuned from the host log by shaking and lifting the unit by hand. A pick-up event is NOT added: lifting looks like the head's own servo reaction on the base, a false pick-up would wake a sleeping robot, and it needs a unit test first.
# Upstream: m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/hal_imu.cpp, hal/utils/motion_detector/motion_detector.h (MIT). Applies after 056 with --unidiff-zero.
# Check after a flash: shake the unit by hand: "unit touch: shake_peak peak=N threshold=9" and a shake reaction; each minute "unit touch: imu_stats max_diff=N shakes=M" shows how hard a lift or a nudge reads.
diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/hal_imu.cpp b/firmware/main/hal/hal_imu.cpp
